Article 2 (Scope of Suspects Whose Fingerprints Shall Be Taken)
(1) Pursuant to Article 2 (2) of the Decree, fingerprints shall be taken when preparing an investigation record card for the following suspects:
1. A suspect of a violation of the Criminal Act;
2. A suspect of a violation of an Act specified in the attached Table.
(2) Even where a suspect does not fall under any subparagraph of paragraph (1), fingerprints shall be taken where:
1. The suspect fails or is unable to present materials proving his or her identity;
2. It is difficult to verify the suspect's identity from the materials presented;
3. The suspect is arrested;
4. It is deemed particularly necessary for investigation and the suspect consents.
(3) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), in a case initiated by complaint or accusation, no investigation record card shall be prepared and no fingerprints shall be taken for a suspect where the disposition not to prosecute is based on any of the following grounds: Provided, That this shall not apply where the suspect falls under paragraph (2) 1, 2, or 4:
1. No suspicion;
2. No right to prosecute;
3. No crime;
4. Dismissal;
5. Suspension of proceedings against a witness. <Newly Inserted on December 31, 1993; June 24, 1995; March 30, 1999>
